{"id": "section-body-01358", "title": "Approach to Dehydrated Patient", "chapterId": "chapter-one", "blocks": [{"id": "body-01358", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Approach to Dehydrated Patient", "runs": [{"text": "Approach"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Dehydrated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Patient"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1855"}}, {"id": "body-01359", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "It refers to the loss of body water, with or without salt at a rate greater than the body can replace it. The cause of dehydration is a combination of physiological and disease processes. Persons at greatest risk for dehydration include persons with diarrhoea, vomiting, fever, diabetes or infections, impaired level status.", "runs": [{"text": "It"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "refers"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "loss"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "body"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "water,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "without"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "salt"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "at"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "greater"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "than"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "body"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "replace"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "it."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "The"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cause"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dehydration is a combination of physiological and disease processes. Persons at greatest risk for dehydration include persons with diarrhoea, vomiting, fever, diabetes or infections, impaired level status."}]}, {"id": "body-01360", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Table 1.3: Types of Dehydration", "runs": [{"text": "Table"}, {"text": "